# Odin 2 for WebCLAP

Odin 2 by TheWaveWarden, a 24-voice polyphonic synthesizer, ported to WebCLAP. This is not an official Odin 2
release.

- Odin 2: https://github.com/TheWaveWarden/odin2 (commit 265e9e2, version 2.4.1)
- This port, and the complete source of this bundle: @SOURCE_URL@
  Build it with `scripts/build-odin2.sh`, which fetches every dependency below at the commit named here and applies
  the changes in `patches/odin2-*.patch`.

## License

The bundle as a whole is licensed under the **GNU Affero General Public License, version 3** (`LICENSE`).

Odin 2 is GPL-3.0-or-later (`licenses/GPL-3.0.txt`), except its Aldrich font. Both modules contain the JUCE framework,
used under the AGPL-3.0, so `module.wasm` and `ui/ui.wasm` are AGPL-3.0. GPL-3.0 section 13 permits the combination.

This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied
warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the licenses for details.

Odin's reverb is adapted from Fons Adriaensen's [zita-rev1](https://github.com/royvegard/zita-rev1) (GPL).

